{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A serpent of copper.</b> Because copper gleams and shines, as it is said: ״ונוצצים כעין נחשת קלל״. And even though the camp of Israel was three parasangs by three parasangs, whoever was bitten could see it from his place." "<b>And he looked at the copper serpent.</b> Because it was placed as a mast on the banner, the bitten person lifts his eyes upward and directs his heart to his Father in heaven, as Rashi explained. And specifically a serpent, and no other creature — to make known the wonders of HaShem, for such are His ways: He strikes with the scalpel and heals with the scalpel."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:18:56.955574812Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}